---
description: Cross-cutting rules for AI Forge — always-on. Defers to `CLAUDE.md` for the full source of truth.
alwaysApply: true
---

AI Forge is a typed, async-first, vendor-neutral baseline for AI/LLM experiments. **Read [`CLAUDE.md`](mdc:CLAUDE.md) before suggesting non-trivial changes.** Module-specific rules live in `src/forge/<module>/CLAUDE.md`.

Always-on rules:

- Public API is async. Sync wrappers live only in `forge.sync`.
- pyright strict on `src/forge`. No `Any` without `# pyright: ignore[...]` justification.
- Errors are exception-based: every Forge-raised error subclasses `forge.core.errors.ForgeError`. Never `except:`.
- Heavy deps (torch, transformers, trl, peft, skypilot, asyncssh, qdrant-client, vllm, pillow, redis, inspect-ai) are imported **inside the function that uses them**, never at module load. Each gates behind a PyPI extra in `pyproject.toml`.
- Commits follow conventional-commit prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `ci:`). Commit messages describe changes in **time-stable terms** — never reference phase numbers, sub-phase numbers, step numbers, or scaffolding metadata.
- **Self-maintenance protocol** (CLAUDE.md §7): when you spot a stale `CLAUDE.md` / MDC rule / ADR / module README, propose the fix in the same PR. Never silently ignore a stale rule.
- Provider SDKs (`anthropic`, `openai`, `google-cloud-aiplatform`, `boto3`) are imported **only inside `src/forge/llm/providers/`**. Everything else goes through `LLMClient` or the `provider_extras` passthrough.
